                  "explanation": "The **Hour-1 Bundle** includes: (1) measure lactate, (2) obtain blood cultures before antibiotics, (3) administer broad-spectrum antibiotics, (4) begin 30 mL/kg crystalloid for hypotension or lactate ≥ 4, (5) start vasopressors if hypotension persists. **Corticosteroids are NOT part of the bundle** and are only considered (typically hydrocortisone 200 mg/day) in **refractory septic shock** requiring escalating vasopressors — not all sepsis patients.",
